Subject: [PATCH 73/73] web-app: custom voice player on by default;
 media-session details setting moves to notifications

The custom voice/audio player has been through four phases of polish and
is the better experience on every surface, so flip
experimentalAudioPlayerControls to true the same way 0061 flipped
experimentalCompletionMenu: change the default in getDefaultState(),
retag the shared-types doc comment, and reword the switch, which stays in
Settings -> Experimental features for anyone who wants the native
<audio> controls back.

Like 0061 this ships no migration, and none is needed: our browser
runtime persists only the keys a user actually touched
(setDesktopSetting writes a single key into slothfulchat.desktopSettings
and getDesktopSettings merges it over the defaults), so a profile that
never met this switch has no stored entry and simply picks up the new
default. That also keeps the key meaningful as a signal -- a stored
false can only come from someone flipping the switch off, never from a
persisted old default, which is what the fork's voice_player_disabled
event counts.

voiceMessageMediaSessionDetails moves out of Experimental features into
Settings -> Notifications, right below "show notification content": it is
the same privacy question in different clothing -- who and which chat is
put on an OS surface that may be a lock screen -- so it belongs next to
the setting people already reason about that way, not filed under
experiments. The key is unchanged, so nothing to migrate. It is greyed
out while the custom player is off (the media session only exists with
the custom player), matching how the row above greys out when
notifications are off.
